## Project Structure Guide

- `app/`: Next.js App Router **pages only** — `app/dashboard/page.tsx` plus nested
  `app/dashboard/statistics/` and `app/dashboard/generator/`, and `about/`,
  `privacy/`, `terms/`. There is no `app/api/`.
- `server.ts`: standalone Bun server owning every `/api/*` endpoint (port 3201).
  `next.config.js` `rewrites()` forwards `/api/:path*` to it. New endpoints go here.
- `proxy.ts`: the Next.js 16 middleware (Next renamed `middleware` → `proxy`); mints
  the per-request CSP nonce and sets page security headers.
- `components/`: reusable UI using Tailwind semantic tokens and shadcn variants.
- `lib/`:
  - `lib/analytics/`: statistics engines and `bet-generator.ts`
  - `lib/api/`: CAIXA API client and response cache
  - `lib/security/`: CSP, HTTP guards, IP pseudonymization
  - `lib/db.ts`: `bun:sqlite` layer; `lib/constants.ts`: shared config (incl. `BASE_URL`)
- `db/`: SQLite database plus `db/migrations/*.sql`.
- `scripts/`: Bun CLIs such as `scripts/pull-draws.ts` for ingest/seeding.
- `tests/`: Vitest (`tests/lib`, `tests/components`, `tests/scripts`) and Playwright
  (`tests/app`).
- `docs/`: DEPLOY, SECURITY, PRIVACY, LGPD-COMPLIANCE, TERMS, INCIDENT-RESPONSE.
  Update `docs/PRIVACY.md` and `docs/LGPD-COMPLIANCE.md` whenever data collection,
  retention, or purpose changes.

Constraints:

- Read `AGENTS.md` first; it is the canonical agent contract for this repo.
- Keep changes minimal and targeted to explicitly requested areas.
- Place new Cursor rules under `.cursor/rules` with the `.mdc` extension.
- User-facing copy is pt-BR.
